1
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:49,966
Hello.

2
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:51,342
- Welcome.
- Thanks.

3
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,510
You're headed to Yeonsinnae, right?

4
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:53,511
Yes.

5
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:56,306
Sorry, but could you hurry just a little?

6
00:00:56,389 --> 00:00:57,557
Yes.

7
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:10,028
You have left the route.
Recalculating.

8
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:15,116
Driver,

9
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,910
Could you follow the GPS, please?

10
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,828
I usually follow the GPS,

11
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:20,830
but you seemed to be in a hurry.

12
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:22,791
I'm taking a route I know.

13
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:25,376
If we take the Inner Ring Road right now,

14
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:28,004
it'll be so backed up,
we could be stuck for ages.

15
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:31,382
You have left the route.
Recalculating.

16
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:38,723
I've been driving taxis for over 40 years.

17
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:41,142
Back before GPS,

18
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:45,605
I had every street and
alley in Seoul memorized.

19
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:50,026
The GPS probably doesn't
even know this road.

20
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:52,946
Driver,

21
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,365
Just follow the GPS, please.

22
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:58,076
All right.

23
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:08,837
Good grief.

24
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:10,839
We're completely stuck.

25
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:29,065
'Recording'

26
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,155
One soft tofu stew!

27
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:36,239
Sure, come on in!

28
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:37,490
Yes.

29
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:39,868
- You're here?
- Oh, you're here?

30
00:02:39,951 --> 00:02:41,244
Yeah.

31
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:49,460
Do you really have to cut
it up every time you eat?

32
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:51,129
Wouldn't it be easier to
cut it all up at once?

33
00:02:51,212 --> 00:02:54,632
If it's all cut up, I can only use a fork.

34
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:57,969
I have to hold a knife in one
hand and a fork in the other

35
00:02:58,052 --> 00:02:59,262
for my pork cutlet to taste better.

36
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:00,305
Yeah, right.

37
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:02,932
You really do like making
things difficult, don't you?

38
00:03:03,516 --> 00:03:07,478
Then again, you do drive
a taxi in an old Mercedes.

39
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:10,732
Oh, right. You don't use
the GPS either, do you?

40
00:03:10,815 --> 00:03:12,775
If you only look at the GPS,

41
00:03:12,859 --> 00:03:15,069
you don't remember the route,
even when you go the same way again.

42
00:03:15,153 --> 00:03:16,613
Exactly.

43
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:17,572
So, today,

44
00:03:17,655 --> 00:03:20,366
I picked up a woman
about my daughter's age,

45
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:24,370
and she really chewed me
out for not using the GPS.

46
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:26,372
But sometimes you take
the long way around.

47
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,499
That was a long time ago.

48
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:31,210
When I was young and foolish,
I tried to make a few extra bucks.

49
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:32,921
I don't do that anymore.

50
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:36,674
These days, passengers sit in the back
with the GPS turned on,

51
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:39,469
watching to make sure
I don't take a detour.

52
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:40,428
Right.

53
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:43,097
It's nice that we're both uncomfortable.

54
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:49,354
Mr. Im,

55
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:51,648
Would you like a bite of pork cutlet?

56
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:53,149
Why?

57
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,193
You want a bite of my soft tofu stew?

58
00:03:58,404 --> 00:04:00,198
That's good.

59
00:04:06,829 --> 00:04:09,040
Man, this really hits the spot.

60
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:13,962
Come on, sir.

61
00:04:14,045 --> 00:04:16,172
What, are you trying to look younger?

62
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:21,386
This isn't mine.

63
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:23,388
Oh, just in time.

64
00:04:23,471 --> 00:04:24,681
Here.

65
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:30,311
Here, take it.

66
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:32,355
Thank you.

67
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:34,774
You seem to be about the same age
as my daughter.

68
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:37,944
My daughter always leaves something
behind in the taxi.

69
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:40,446
Right, well, the battery was dead,

70
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:41,364
so I charged it all the way.

71
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:43,241
Oh, sir.

72
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:46,452
You say 'filled it up' for gas.
Who says that these days?

73
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:48,413
Thank you.

74
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:50,373
Also,

75
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,501
I'm really sorry about this morning.

76
00:04:53,584 --> 00:04:56,337
I should've listened to you. I didn't think
we'd get stuck in traffic like that...

77
00:04:58,089 --> 00:05:00,425
Well, how about a bite of pork cutlet
before you go?

78
00:05:00,508 --> 00:05:02,510
No, I'm fine.

79
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:05,179
Here you go. Come again.

80
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,889
- Thanks for the meal.
- Thank you.

81
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:12,520
Here.

82
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:14,022
Thank you.

83
00:05:20,611 --> 00:05:21,863
Wow.

84
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:23,197
You're thrifty.

85
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:25,325
This?

86
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:27,243
It's for my wife.

87
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:30,705
If I bring her a whole bag,
she eats it all in one day.

88
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,966
Mr. Im even buys us meals,

89
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,844
and earlier, he wouldn't even take a tip.

90
00:05:44,927 --> 00:05:45,887
Did he win the lottery?

91
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:50,558
We'll be getting plenty of wedding
gifts this week, so it's fine.

92
00:05:50,641 --> 00:05:52,769
- Wedding gifts?
- Yeah, this weekend

93
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:54,771
my youngest daughter is getting married.

94
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:56,606
Come by, have a meal, and celebrate.

95
00:05:57,648 --> 00:06:00,735
You're telling me to
give you a wedding gift.

96
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:05,990
Instead of a wedding gift,
could you pick me up in the morning?

97
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:10,411
Today's booked passengers are

98
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:12,914
Mr. Im, a taxi driver.

99
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:15,708
I've known him for a long time.

100
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:19,462
Today is the wedding of
Mr. Im's youngest daughter.

101
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:20,630
Instead of giving a wedding gift,

102
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:23,424
I've offered to take the two of
them safely to the wedding venue.

103
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:27,512
I should still give them
a wedding gift, right?

104
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:33,226
- You're here?
- Yes.

105
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:35,561
I've heard a lot about you.

106
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:37,939
You came so early.

107
00:06:38,022 --> 00:06:40,691
- Thank you.
- Don't mention it.

108
00:06:40,775 --> 00:06:43,444
When I first started driving a
taxi, Mr. Im

109
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:44,529
helped me out a lot.

110
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:46,030
- Not at all.
- Not at all...

111
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:47,532
Please, get in.

112
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:49,117
- Go ahead.
- Sure.

113
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:04,799
Seula, that sleepyhead,

114
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:08,344
left at the crack of dawn to
get her bridal makeup done.

115
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:15,435
When did our little girl grow up so much?

116
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:17,728
Time just flew by.

117
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:21,023
It's my wedding. I can't sleep in.

118
00:07:22,358 --> 00:07:26,487
I told her to at least have a bite,
but she left without even looking at me.

119
00:07:28,072 --> 00:07:30,116
When you got married,
you were worried about gaining weight,

120
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:31,617
and wouldn't even drink a glass of water.

121
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:34,078
Do you think Seula would eat breakfast?

122
00:07:34,662 --> 00:07:36,330
Keep your voice down.

123
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:39,876
You can fix it when we get there.

124
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:42,462
No, lots of people will be there,

125
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:44,088
and the in-laws will talk.

126
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:47,967
I'm not the one getting married.
What's wrong with a crooked tie?

127
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:48,968
Who's looking at me?

128
00:07:50,636 --> 00:07:51,679
That's just how he is.

129
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:55,183
Still,

130
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:57,602
when Mrs. Im isn't around,

131
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:59,896
he takes such good care of her.

132
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:03,232
He even brought peppermint candy.

133
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:04,525
Yes.

134
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:05,443
Peppermint candy?

135
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:09,697
By the way, Mr. Ko, how much farther?

136
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,199
We're almost there.

137
00:08:14,285 --> 00:08:15,703
You aren't sitting over there by yourself.

138
00:08:15,786 --> 00:08:19,081
This is our first time sitting side
by side in the back seat, isn't it?

139
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:19,999
Come to think of it,

140
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:24,337
Don't you remember?
We first met in the back of a taxi.

141
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:36,057
Excuse me, Sir.
I'm going to pick up another passenger.

142
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:39,727
- Sure.
- Thank you.

143
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:44,398
Back then, it was common to share a taxi.

144
00:08:44,482 --> 00:08:45,942
Even if there was already a passenger,

145
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:46,984
Driver, Dongdaemun, please.

146
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:48,236
Sure, we're headed that way. Hop in.

147
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:49,612
- If they were going in the same direction...
- Thank you.

148
00:08:49,695 --> 00:08:51,572
they'd pick up another passenger.

149
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:53,491
All right, we're off.

150
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:03,626
I'm picking up another passenger.

151
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:07,838
Listen, driver, I'm a taxi driver too,

152
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:10,341
but isn't it a bit much to pick up someone
while we're already sharing a taxi?

153
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:13,302
There's still one seat left.
Let's fill it.

154
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:15,263
In a country that doesn't
produce a drop of oil,

155
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:20,017
Right.

156
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:24,647
Welcome aboard.

157
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:26,399
- Hello.
- Where are you headed?

158
00:09:26,482 --> 00:09:28,234
- Euljiro 3-ga, please.
- Sure.

159
00:09:28,317 --> 00:09:30,319
You can get off with the
passenger in the back.

160
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,446
We're off.

161
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:52,008
I don't live in Seoul, so...

162
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:55,845
Do you know where this
place on the map is?

163
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:03,811
Follow me. I know a shortcut.

164
00:10:04,478 --> 00:10:05,938
Oh, no.

165
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:07,773
You don't have to go out of
your way to come with me.

166
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:10,776
No, no. I'm going that way too.

167
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,445
- All right.
- It's no trouble.

168
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:14,530
- Shall we go?
- Thank you.

169
00:10:22,288 --> 00:10:23,748
I'm sorry I didn't recognize you.

170
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,501
Not at all.

171
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:31,130
It's my first blind date.

172
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:35,885
I should've told you what
I looked like beforehand.

173
00:10:35,968 --> 00:10:37,303
Yes.

174
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:42,808
You're good at finding
your way with just a map.

175
00:10:43,392 --> 00:10:45,269
I'm a taxi driver.

176
00:10:45,353 --> 00:10:47,188
Finding my way around is my job.

177
00:10:47,271 --> 00:10:50,316
Well, just about every
road and alley in Seoul

178
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:52,652
is all in my head, you could say.

179
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:03,162
Driver.

180
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:05,373
Yes?

181
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:08,417
Please pull over.

182
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:13,130
Please let me out, driver.

183
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:15,508
Please let me out, okay?

184
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:18,219
Please let me out.

185
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:19,387
Wait a second...

186
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:35,403
- Well...
- Please let me out.

187
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:38,197
Let me out.

188
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:43,452
Who are you?

189
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:48,165
I'm your husband.

190
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:53,879
Yes.

191
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:56,841
Before we left, Driver Im

192
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:58,926
gave me a CD.

193
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,011
Driver Ko.

194
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:02,471
- Yes.
- Wait.

195
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:03,597
This.

196
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:06,434
When I give you the signal, play this.

197
00:12:06,517 --> 00:12:08,561
- Yes, sir.
- Every now and then...

198
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:40,342
♪ The wind is blowing ♪

199
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:48,809
♪ Aren't you cold? ♪

200
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:53,189
♪ The night grows late ♪

201
00:12:53,856 --> 00:12:59,028
♪ Suddenly, your face ♪

202
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,617
♪ Comes to mind ♪

203
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:16,128
♪ Your smile made my heart race ♪

204
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:20,591
♪ Your trembling voice ♪

205
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:22,384
All right, let's go.

206
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:25,596
Okay, look at the camera.
Come on, come on.

207
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:27,973
Okay, smile, smile, smile.
Smile.

208
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:29,767
♪ Through so many wounds ♪

209
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:35,397
♪ My frozen heart ♪

210
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:40,069
♪ Was wrapped in ♪

211
00:13:42,613 --> 00:13:46,116
♪ Life is ♪

212
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,118
♪ A mysterious blessing ♪

213
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,372
Okay, look this way.

214
00:13:51,455 --> 00:13:53,207
One, two, three!

215
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:54,416
Oh, coming all this way...

216
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,960
♪ There's a clear reason ♪

217
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,508
♪ In this world ♪

218
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:05,886
♪ No one is unnecessary... ♪

219
00:14:07,721 --> 00:14:08,847
You.

220
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:10,432
You mustn't forget this moment.

221
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,352
The day I got my first taxi

222
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:16,897
We had a blessing ceremony for it,
then, while we were eating boiled pork...

223
00:14:18,857 --> 00:14:21,402
That's when your morning
sickness started, right?

224
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:26,574
♪ And face each other ♪

225
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:28,158
Honey, thank you.

226
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:31,370
♪ First born ♪

227
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:38,961
This good-for-nothing...

228
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:43,465
I made you work so hard
when you were young.

229
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:45,342
I didn't bring home much money.

230
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:47,595
I was always coming home late.

231
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:50,973
But you raised the kids so well.

232
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:55,227
You made this family what it is.

233
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:57,855
Of everyone in our family,

234
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:00,566
the most precious person

235
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:03,152
is you.

236
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:01,877
You did great.

237
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:14,431
You look so beautiful. Congratulations.

238
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:20,604
- I'll get going.
- Okay.

239
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:21,897
Hello, ma'am.

240
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:23,065
Yes.

241
00:16:43,168 --> 00:16:44,169
Congratulations.

242
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:51,760
I'm sorry.

243
00:17:02,604 --> 00:17:04,189
Mom's memories

244
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:09,278
are all right here.

245
00:17:52,654 --> 00:17:55,574
♪ To be alive ♪

246
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:58,077
♪ Is a mysterious blessing ♪

247
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:02,581
♪ There's a clear ♪

248
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:06,210
♪ Reason for it ♪

249
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:12,216
♪ In this world ♪

250
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:15,969
♪ There's no one ♪

251
00:18:17,429 --> 00:18:19,932
♪ Who isn't needed ♪

252
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:22,309
♪ Everyone ♪

253
00:18:24,978 --> 00:18:29,191
♪ Open your heart ♪

254
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:34,822
♪ And ♪

255
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:37,825
♪ Face each other ♪

256
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:46,250
♪ On this planet where
we were first born ♪

257
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:49,586
♪ We who live here ♪

258
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:52,256
♪ Let's join hands ♪

259
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:53,924
The couple getting married today,

260
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:55,759
the groom, Jang Dong-won,

261
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:58,387
and the bride, Im Seul-a,

262
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:00,097
I, as their officiant, sincerely...

263
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,141
♪ On this planet ♪

264
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:03,725
♪ We who live here... ♪

265
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:05,519
The bride and groom
standing here

266
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:07,521
to get to this day

267
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:09,857
were born and raised by

268
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:13,443
the parents of both families, who brought
them together and saw them married,

269
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,821
for all your devotion...

270
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:35,299
The song you just heard was

271
00:19:35,382 --> 00:19:38,302
The Beatles' 'A Day in the Life.'

272
00:19:38,385 --> 00:19:41,346
It's the final track
on the album.

273
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:42,931
At the end of the song,

274
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:45,017
they say there's a
sound humans can't hear,

275
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:48,729
recorded at a frequency
only dogs can hear.

276
00:19:49,938 --> 00:19:54,318
So does that mean no one on Earth
has ever heard the whole song

277
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:55,736
all the way to the end?

278
00:19:55,819 --> 00:19:57,321
Well, anyway, that's how it is.

279
00:19:58,614 --> 00:20:00,532
You're listening to Bae
Chul-soo's Music Camp.

280
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:03,911
Today's show is all about
your song requests.

281
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:06,330
Here's a message from 8380.

282
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:09,583
'I drive a taxi.'

283
00:20:09,666 --> 00:20:10,500
'When I pick up passengers, '

284
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:12,002
'on the way to their destination, '

285
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:15,088
'I play the songs they request.'

286
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:18,884
'I'm always taking song requests
from my passengers, '

287
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:22,679
'but today, I'd like to send in
my own request to you, Chul-soo.'

288
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:26,767
This person is a taxi driver.

289
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:29,394
So you do something similar to me.

290
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:30,979
You've got a DJ's blood

291
00:20:31,063 --> 00:20:32,731
running through your veins.

292
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:35,943
'I didn't always take song requests.'

293
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:37,819
'I started taking requests when...'

294
00:20:56,421 --> 00:20:58,840
So that's the story behind it.

295
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:01,510
To the person who texted 8380,

296
00:21:01,593 --> 00:21:04,554
keep playing great music
for the passengers who get in your taxi,

297
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,014
and treat them to plenty of good songs.

298
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:06,932
Yes.

299
00:21:07,015 --> 00:21:08,183
And please send lots of requests

300
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:09,768
to our show, Music Camp, too.

301
00:21:09,851 --> 00:21:10,686
I will!

302
00:21:10,769 --> 00:21:14,398
Now, the song requested by 8380...

303
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:17,734
This person...

304
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:21,655
didn't actually include
their own song request.

305
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:24,825
We'll take a commercial break.

306
00:21:24,908 --> 00:21:28,412
Every day, we share the same spaces.

307
00:21:28,495 --> 00:21:30,706
On the streets and on public transit,

308
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:33,667
and throughout our daily lives.

309
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:35,335
If we show a little more consideration,

310
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:37,421
Someone's day
can be much safer.
